Yes, pandoc is really an amazing piece of software, so instead of
mk4ht/htlatex, I prefer markdown + knitr + pandoc --> HTML/PDF/...

I'm also thinking on simplifying the default R code syntax for
markdown: <!--begin.rcode and end.rcode--> are too long to write, and
I want to leave them in HTML only; markdown can use patterns like four
spaces indent followed by chunk options.

This is actually something I planned to do in GSoC:
http://rwiki.sciviews.org/doku.php?id=developers:projects:gsoc2012:knitr
but I'm afraid it can be done before that because it does not seem to
be hard... BTW, is anyone interested in becoming the second mentor of
this GSoC project? I believe we will end up with lots of cool
applications. I have already got a student.

